# Repo map

One git repo, several separate projects. They share a research goal (Torino UBEM with provenance, `paper2/`) but they are not one codebase. They connect through the database, exported files, and papers — never through cross-project Python imports.

## Runtime projects

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `city_information_modeler/` | **Active development.** Stateless `core/`, external `parallel/` runner, `app/` orchestration, `notebooks/`, `config/`. All new work goes here. |
| `cim_wizard_integrated_2026/` | **Frozen.** Previous backend: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Celery + PostGIS, plus `building_simulation/` (CESAR-P), `grid_simulation/`, `logic/*.ipynb`, `alembic/`. Read for reference; do not change. |
| `cim-database/` | Database stack: PostgreSQL, PostGIS, TimescaleDB, 3DCityDB with Energy ADE. Init SQL, migrations, TABULA data, ER diagrams. |
| `datalake/` | Semi data warehouse (objective O1). Streamlit ingest wizard + FastAPI over PostGIS; separate DB from `cim-database`. |
| `coesi-frontend-main_2026/` | Web client. React 19, Vite, TypeScript, MapLibre. |
| `semantic/` | Ontology and OBDA layer: Ontop mappings, Fuseki/GraphDB compose, CityGML + BOT + SOSA + GeoSPARQL. |

## CIM Assist (one project, three stages)

| Path | Stage |
|---|---|
| `ai4db/` | Build the CIM spatial text-to-SQL dataset and benchmark. |
| `txt2ssql/` | Fine-tune the models (`ftv2/`, `ftv3/`: SQLCoder, Qwen, Llama, Mistral, Phi). |
| `assist_cim/` | Agent, evaluation (`evaluator_v2.py`), figures and tables. |

## Research and data folders

- `paper2/` — Paper 2 outline and LaTeX. Objectives O1–O7 name their implementation folder; read it before changing a claim.
- `thesis_CIM_wizard_Assist/` — MSc thesis behind CIM Assist.
- `cosimulation/` — mosaik sandbox. Not wired into the API; the existing building simulation code sits in the frozen `cim_wizard_integrated_2026/building_simulation/`, so rebuild rather than edit it.
- `phd_proposal/` — reference PDFs only.
- `grid/`, `pv/` — geodata only (substation borders, PV footprints). Grid and PV code belongs in the backend, not here.

## Boundaries

- Keep a change inside one project. Do not import across project folders; move shared logic into the backend or pass data through the database or a file.
- The other rules in `.cursor/rules/` target `city_information_modeler/` unless their `globs` say otherwise. Its layers and the stateless, parallelizable core contract are in the `cim-development-structure` rule.
- Data-only folders stay data-only. Do not add scripts to `grid/`, `pv/`, or `phd_proposal/`.
